261
00:14:38,544 --> 00:14:39,712
Mongolia,

262
00:14:40,212 --> 00:14:41,714
and the Philippines.

263
00:14:45,426 --> 00:14:46,802
A rematch between the Republic of Korea…

264
00:14:46,886 --> 00:14:47,720
Okay.

265
00:14:48,512 --> 00:14:50,472
…and Türkiye.

266
00:14:54,727 --> 00:14:55,644
Stand by.

267
00:14:58,731 --> 00:14:59,899
Ready…

268
00:15:07,656 --> 00:15:08,741
Go for the female players!

269
00:15:12,286 --> 00:15:13,621
Go for the female players!

270
00:15:20,210 --> 00:15:22,254
I mean, the sheer strength of those guys…

271
00:15:24,173 --> 00:15:27,051
Wow, I mean, seriously,

272
00:15:27,134 --> 00:15:28,344
it was unmatched.

273
00:15:33,766 --> 00:15:34,767
Seung-yeon.

274
00:15:35,684 --> 00:15:37,353
Hold off for now.

275
00:15:37,436 --> 00:15:39,730
Just wait it out.

276
00:15:41,649 --> 00:15:44,902
A guy that big trying to fight two women?

277
00:15:44,985 --> 00:15:47,154
-They'll be too scared to go in.
-What's going on?

278
00:15:47,237 --> 00:15:49,990
But Korea needs to fight, or they're out.

279
00:15:50,074 --> 00:15:51,241
Yes, this is pointless.

280
00:15:51,825 --> 00:15:52,785
Grab the women.

281
00:15:52,868 --> 00:15:54,495
Watch out, two of them are outside!

282
00:15:55,162 --> 00:15:56,580
Two of them are outside.

283
00:15:57,331 --> 00:15:58,540
Thirty-eight seconds!

284
00:16:01,460 --> 00:16:02,628
Sung-bin, come over here.

285
00:16:02,711 --> 00:16:04,672
Come over here and hold onto me.

286
00:16:06,173 --> 00:16:08,842
Lie down, lie down.

287
00:16:08,926 --> 00:16:10,427
Everyone, link up.

288
00:16:10,511 --> 00:16:11,637
Hold my hand.

289
00:16:11,720 --> 00:16:14,264
Lie down and link arms.

290
00:16:14,974 --> 00:16:16,100
Let them fight.

291
00:16:17,476 --> 00:16:18,477
That's okay.

292
00:16:20,521 --> 00:16:22,147
No need to rush.
Let Indonesia set themselves up.

293
00:16:22,231 --> 00:16:23,524
Hold your horses, guys.

294
00:16:24,441 --> 00:16:27,069
They've sat down. I'm going in. Just wait.

295
00:16:27,152 --> 00:16:29,863
-Is there two teams against this one team?
-They're going in for the peel now.

296
00:16:30,948 --> 00:16:33,534
They got heavier competitors.
Now they're gonna pick them off.

297
00:16:34,368 --> 00:16:37,579
Lie down and link arms.

298
00:16:37,663 --> 00:16:40,582
-Be careful, they could drag us off.
-Lie down.

299
00:16:40,666 --> 00:16:43,002
-Pick off one or two.
-Come on!

300
00:16:43,085 --> 00:16:45,129
-Pull them out!
-Come on!

301
00:16:45,212 --> 00:16:47,881
Drag them down.

302
00:16:47,965 --> 00:16:50,300
Drag them down this way.

303
00:16:50,384 --> 00:16:52,177
No, no.

304
00:16:53,137 --> 00:16:55,764
Glenn, hold tight.

305
00:16:57,766 --> 00:16:59,018
Thirty seconds.

306
00:17:02,062 --> 00:17:03,313
Seung-yeon, come over here.

307
00:17:03,397 --> 00:17:05,190
I think Türkiye's game plan

308
00:17:05,274 --> 00:17:08,444
was to stop the women
from climbing onto the territory.

309
00:17:11,155 --> 00:17:12,322
Sung-bin, did everyone make it up?

310
00:17:12,406 --> 00:17:13,449
Hold on to the girls.

311
00:17:13,532 --> 00:17:16,243
Pull off the men.
The women aren't on here!

312
00:17:18,579 --> 00:17:19,830
Push.

313
00:17:21,331 --> 00:17:22,374
Push.

314
00:17:27,713 --> 00:17:30,257
Korea's the team with the most experience

315
00:17:30,340 --> 00:17:32,509
and a strong contender to win.

316
00:17:32,593 --> 00:17:34,678
They're different from the other teams.

317
00:17:35,763 --> 00:17:38,849
Get in. Hold on tight. Hold here.

318
00:17:38,932 --> 00:17:41,310
Pull off the men.
The women aren't on here!

319
00:17:46,440 --> 00:17:49,651
They kept attacking us,
but we couldn't possibly lose to them.

320
00:17:49,735 --> 00:17:52,112
So we just fought back blindly
with sheer grit.

321
00:18:08,003 --> 00:18:10,255
All right, charge! Khandsuren, charge!

322
00:18:10,339 --> 00:18:14,301
-Khandsuren, over here!
-Khandsuren, charge!

323
00:18:14,384 --> 00:18:15,511
Glenn, hold tight.

324
00:18:15,594 --> 00:18:17,137
If my leg falls out, I'm a goner.

325
00:18:17,221 --> 00:18:18,764
Glenn, hold on tight, like this.

326
00:18:18,847 --> 00:18:21,266
We're gonna get really low, okay?
Really low.

327
00:18:21,350 --> 00:18:22,935
-You ready? Go! Come on, now!
-Come on.

328
00:18:23,018 --> 00:18:23,852
Wait.

329
00:18:24,353 --> 00:18:25,312
Jeepney blitz!

330
00:18:28,023 --> 00:18:29,817
Oh, they're rucking.

331
00:18:29,900 --> 00:18:31,401
They can't ruck, they're lying down.

332
00:18:31,485 --> 00:18:33,862
-Get in there.
-Get in there!

333
00:18:33,946 --> 00:18:35,239
Get in and fight!

334
00:18:35,864 --> 00:18:36,990
Ten seconds.

335
00:18:38,033 --> 00:18:40,994
All right, now! Three, two, one, charge!

336
00:18:56,468 --> 00:18:59,179
I tried my best in that moment.

337
00:19:01,557 --> 00:19:02,850
Ten seconds.

338
00:19:03,517 --> 00:19:05,185
Come on, you've got to come!

339
00:19:06,311 --> 00:19:08,647
Min-jae, push off one more! Three seconds!

340
00:19:26,081 --> 00:19:27,958
Stop. Game over.

341
00:19:28,041 --> 00:19:28,876
I'm still on here.

342
00:19:28,959 --> 00:19:30,794
-Over here.
-All right!

343
00:19:30,878 --> 00:19:33,505
I'm still on here. I'm on the territory.

344
00:19:33,589 --> 00:19:36,133
No, same. No.

345
00:19:38,552 --> 00:19:41,388
We pushed one of the Indonesians off
right at the end.

346
00:19:41,471 --> 00:19:43,056
-Really?
-Yeah, one of them.

347
00:19:43,140 --> 00:19:44,933
-Indonesia?
-Yeah, one Indonesian.

348
00:19:49,313 --> 00:19:50,272
Rematch.

349
00:19:51,773 --> 00:19:53,859
The Republic of Korea and Türkiye.

350
00:19:56,653 --> 00:19:57,529
All right!

351
00:19:58,030 --> 00:19:59,573
Yes!

352
00:19:59,656 --> 00:20:02,284
-Did we win?
-No, it's a rematch.

353
00:20:03,285 --> 00:20:04,244
Rematch.

354
00:20:07,623 --> 00:20:09,958
Mongolia and the Philippines.

355
00:20:12,628 --> 00:20:14,713
-Yup, that's us, Philippines.
-Mongolia, Philippines,

356
00:20:14,796 --> 00:20:15,672
they just said, right?

357
00:20:15,756 --> 00:20:19,426
It is what it is.
We need to accept the result.

358
00:20:22,846 --> 00:20:25,641
The second rematch will now begin.

359
00:20:26,892 --> 00:20:28,227
You will fight over

360
00:20:29,394 --> 00:20:30,437
a single territory.

361
00:20:31,438 --> 00:20:34,358
Of the four countries
involved in the rematch,

362
00:20:34,441 --> 00:20:36,610
only two will advance to the second round.

363
00:20:36,693 --> 00:20:39,613
-Come on, let's go. Bring it home!
-Come on!

364
00:20:43,533 --> 00:20:45,786
The game will last for one minute.

365
00:20:48,121 --> 00:20:50,374
I was trying to figure out our approach.

366
00:20:52,209 --> 00:20:55,504
We need to come up with a good strategy.

367
00:20:55,587 --> 00:21:00,634
We have many tricks up our sleeve
aside from the jeepney blitz.

368
00:21:00,717 --> 00:21:06,974
So Justin approached the Mongolians,
asking them to team up with us

369
00:21:07,057 --> 00:21:12,062
so we could strengthen the power
of the jeepney blitz.

370
00:21:19,403 --> 00:21:20,696
Stand by.

371
00:21:24,908 --> 00:21:25,951
Ready…

372
00:21:31,373 --> 00:21:33,250
Let's go! Come on!

373
00:21:38,297 --> 00:21:40,090
-Let's go.
-Go!

374
00:21:40,924 --> 00:21:42,175
Let's go.

375
00:21:42,259 --> 00:21:43,468
Ogeday.

376
00:21:48,765 --> 00:21:51,268
Oh, Türkiye… Oh my gosh.

377
00:21:51,351 --> 00:21:53,020
-Come on.
-It's this one.

378
00:21:53,103 --> 00:21:54,271
-Get up here.
-Pack in.

379
00:21:54,938 --> 00:21:58,191
-Come on. Get up here.
-Pack in. Come on.

380
00:21:58,275 --> 00:21:59,651
Come on, take your spots.

381
00:22:02,529 --> 00:22:04,323
-They've teamed up.
-Those two have teamed up.

382
00:22:04,865 --> 00:22:05,991
They've teamed up.

383
00:22:07,075 --> 00:22:08,493
No way.

384
00:22:09,369 --> 00:22:12,205
Join, join. Mongolia, Mongolia!

385
00:22:12,289 --> 00:22:13,874
Hey, over here.

386
00:22:13,957 --> 00:22:15,959
Everyone, this way. Let's go!

387
00:22:18,253 --> 00:22:19,463
What's going on?

388
00:22:19,546 --> 00:22:20,881
It's an attack on Mongolia
and the Philippines.

389
00:22:20,964 --> 00:22:21,923
Is that what's happening?

390
00:22:22,966 --> 00:22:25,469
10 MINUTES AGO

391
00:22:25,552 --> 00:22:26,970
-This round, two teams.
-Yeah.

392
00:22:27,054 --> 00:22:28,221
-Two teams will go up.
-Two teams go up.

393
00:22:28,305 --> 00:22:29,181
We work together, yeah?

394
00:22:29,264 --> 00:22:31,433
-Together?
-Yeah, cool.

395
00:22:31,516 --> 00:22:32,476
-Really?
-Yeah.

396
00:22:32,559 --> 00:22:35,854
-"We're no strangers," okay?
-Oh, yeah.

397
00:22:35,937 --> 00:22:37,022
Teaming up.

398
00:22:38,106 --> 00:22:40,108
-They're gonna be teaming up.
-Yeah, for sure.

399
00:22:40,192 --> 00:22:44,654
What I noticed was, I looked to my left
and I see Amotti and Dong-hyun Kim

400
00:22:44,738 --> 00:22:47,074
walk over to the Turkish team.

401
00:22:47,157 --> 00:22:50,202
And I could tell.
At that moment, I looked at our team,

402
00:22:50,285 --> 00:22:52,871
I said, "Look, we need to
team up with Mongolia."

403
00:22:54,164 --> 00:22:56,249
Over here, over here. Hey!

404
00:22:56,333 --> 00:22:57,542
Come.

405
00:22:58,335 --> 00:22:59,753
Thirty seconds.

406
00:23:01,171 --> 00:23:02,464
-This way.
-This way.

407
00:23:02,547 --> 00:23:03,673
Turn.

408
00:23:03,757 --> 00:23:06,259
Turn, turn.

409
00:23:07,677 --> 00:23:10,972
-Pack in. Huddle up!
-Turn, turn.

410
00:23:11,640 --> 00:23:14,768
We sent the girls behind us,
and we asked them to stand behind us,

411
00:23:14,851 --> 00:23:19,439
support us like a pillar,
and push us from the back.

412
00:23:19,523 --> 00:23:22,901
And other men would hold onto them
from behind and protect them.

413
00:23:22,984 --> 00:23:26,738
With a three-layer structure like that,
we'd be invincible.

414
00:23:26,822 --> 00:23:28,824
-Build it now.
-Let's get ready.

415
00:23:28,907 --> 00:23:30,200
Move as one. Get down.

416
00:23:30,283 --> 00:23:32,077
Link up. Build it.

417
00:23:32,160 --> 00:23:33,787
-Keep moving.
-Link up. Build it.

418
00:23:33,870 --> 00:23:37,249
Fifteen! At fifteen seconds to go!

419
00:23:37,332 --> 00:23:39,584
A scrum is really, really technical.

420
00:23:39,668 --> 00:23:40,752
But we made our way,

421
00:23:40,836 --> 00:23:44,005
and there were language barriers,
as there is with different countries.

422
00:23:44,089 --> 00:23:48,301
We agreed that we would form
a joint scrum, a joint jeepney,

423
00:23:48,385 --> 00:23:52,055
and blitz with about
20 to 15 seconds to go.

424
00:23:52,139 --> 00:23:54,683
-Go early!
-Come on!

425
00:23:54,766 --> 00:23:56,810
-Push them out!
-Early, go, go!

426
00:24:02,858 --> 00:24:04,609
-Twenty seconds!
-Twenty.

427
00:24:04,693 --> 00:24:07,070
Let's go, left turn.

428
00:24:12,200 --> 00:24:13,285
-Fifteen.
-Let's go!

429
00:24:13,368 --> 00:24:15,537
-Let's go!
-Let's go!

430
00:24:29,551 --> 00:24:31,011
Ten seconds.

431
00:24:38,435 --> 00:24:41,897
Pack in, pack in!

432
00:24:45,650 --> 00:24:49,196
Pack in, pack in!

433
00:24:49,738 --> 00:24:52,741
Get up here!

434
00:24:52,824 --> 00:24:54,951
Five seconds! Four! Three!

435
00:25:01,791 --> 00:25:02,918
Stop.

436
00:25:05,170 --> 00:25:07,297
Stop. Game over.

437
00:25:17,849 --> 00:25:19,267
-What happened?
-I don't know, I couldn't see.

438
00:25:20,852 --> 00:25:22,062
Was there anyone else out?

439
00:25:23,730 --> 00:25:25,106
I was on it when the whistle blew.

440
00:25:25,190 --> 00:25:27,734
-Yeah?
-I got thrown out afterward.

441
00:25:28,360 --> 00:25:29,778
That was incredible.

442
00:25:29,861 --> 00:25:32,322
-They teamed up, right?
-That's not a bad strategy.

443
00:25:33,657 --> 00:25:34,658
Rematch.

444
00:25:35,492 --> 00:25:36,493
The Republic of Korea,

445
00:25:37,786 --> 00:25:38,662
Mongolia,

446
00:25:40,580 --> 00:25:41,539
and…

447
00:25:49,381 --> 00:25:51,508
Stop. Game over.

448
00:25:53,593 --> 00:25:55,220
…and Türkiye.

449
00:25:55,303 --> 00:25:57,597
-Yes!
-Come on!

450
00:25:57,681 --> 00:26:01,476
So it's just the three teams.

451
00:26:02,102 --> 00:26:04,896
It was just pure disappointment.

452
00:26:04,980 --> 00:26:06,439
JUSTIN COVENEY
NATIONAL TEAM RUGBY PLAYER

453
00:26:06,523 --> 00:26:09,484
It was a really,
sort of depressing moment.

454
00:26:12,821 --> 00:26:15,699
The third rematch will now begin.

455
00:26:16,783 --> 00:26:18,118
You will fight over

456
00:26:18,702 --> 00:26:19,703
a single territory.

457
00:26:22,205 --> 00:26:23,665
Mongolia's gonna be teamed up on.

458
00:26:23,748 --> 00:26:25,083
Yeah, they're gonna get slaughtered.

459
00:26:26,334 --> 00:26:29,212
After beating the Philippines,
I knew that Korea and Türkiye

460
00:26:29,296 --> 00:26:32,549
would form an alliance
in the upcoming game.

461
00:26:34,467 --> 00:26:36,344
The only choice we had was to fight.

462
00:26:43,893 --> 00:26:45,020
All right!

463
00:26:45,103 --> 00:26:47,272
Everyone, hold back and don't rush.

464
00:26:48,273 --> 00:26:49,607
They're gonna do the same tactic.

465
00:26:50,233 --> 00:26:51,818
It's two teams against one.

466
00:26:54,946 --> 00:26:58,450
If we fight with everything we've got…

467
00:27:00,744 --> 00:27:03,371
it'll be an epic showdown with no regrets.

468
00:27:04,622 --> 00:27:06,166
Get him out. Drag him out.

469
00:27:09,294 --> 00:27:11,921
We, the Mongolians,
went harder than anyone else.

470
00:27:14,049 --> 00:27:15,633
We were formidable.

471
00:27:17,969 --> 00:27:19,012
Hey, help me!

472
00:27:22,390 --> 00:27:23,975
We're going in now. Let's go!

473
00:27:28,688 --> 00:27:31,524
Hey! Get ready, everyone!

474
00:27:33,610 --> 00:27:35,695
-Ten seconds!
-Ten seconds!

475
00:27:35,779 --> 00:27:36,863
Everyone, get in!

476
00:27:41,076 --> 00:27:42,786
-Five! Four!
-Five! Four!

477
00:27:42,869 --> 00:27:44,746
Go!

478
00:27:45,705 --> 00:27:46,998
Three! Two!

479
00:27:48,666 --> 00:27:49,876
-One!
-Get in!

480
00:27:54,381 --> 00:27:55,465
Game over.

481
00:27:56,132 --> 00:27:57,133
Mongolia?

482
00:27:58,051 --> 00:27:59,302
Is Team Korea out?

483
00:28:03,932 --> 00:28:06,226
Here are the countries
surviving after the first round.

484
00:28:06,309 --> 00:28:07,477
The Republic of Korea

485
00:28:07,560 --> 00:28:08,686
and Türkiye.

486
00:28:10,271 --> 00:28:11,356
We did so well.

487
00:28:13,108 --> 00:28:16,152
Our team could've done so much better.

488
00:28:16,236 --> 00:28:18,363
That was a really disappointing game.

489
00:28:20,281 --> 00:28:22,117
Here are the results
of the first round's rematch.

490
00:28:22,200 --> 00:28:23,952
The countries advancing
to the second round

491
00:28:24,035 --> 00:28:27,247
are Japan, Australia, Türkiye,
and the Republic of Korea.

492
00:28:28,498 --> 00:28:30,083
Physical: Asia.

493
00:28:30,166 --> 00:28:32,710
Second round of the territory conquest.

494
00:28:34,087 --> 00:28:36,047
You will fight to conquer

495
00:28:36,131 --> 00:28:37,549
two territories.

496
00:28:39,884 --> 00:28:44,431
You will now select your starting points.

497
00:28:45,056 --> 00:28:46,391
Let's go straight for Australia.

498
00:28:46,474 --> 00:28:47,517
We charge into them.

499
00:28:47,600 --> 00:28:49,978
-Good idea.
-Let's give it to them in full force.

500
00:28:50,061 --> 00:28:52,397
We immediately targeted Australia…

501
00:28:52,480 --> 00:28:53,815
RECEP KARA
FORMER NATIONAL TEAM OIL WRESTLER

502
00:28:53,898 --> 00:28:55,358
…for a direct face-off.

503
00:28:55,442 --> 00:28:56,443
It was go hard or go home.

504
00:28:57,110 --> 00:28:58,820
"You really think you can beat us?"

505
00:28:58,903 --> 00:29:01,364
"No one can take us on."
That was their attitude.

506
00:29:02,073 --> 00:29:03,283
That's what I heard them say.

507
00:29:04,075 --> 00:29:06,119
No one came.

508
00:29:06,870 --> 00:29:08,079
Okay, next turn.

509
00:29:08,163 --> 00:29:10,832
Next turn, you versus us, okay?
Easy money.

510
00:29:10,915 --> 00:29:13,710
-Easy money, bro.
-Okay. Easy money, yeah.

511
00:29:13,793 --> 00:29:14,753
You don't want this smoke.

512
00:29:14,836 --> 00:29:16,546
No one wanted this smoke.

513
00:29:17,130 --> 00:29:21,468
They may look intimidating,
but they're actually easy prey.

514
00:29:21,551 --> 00:29:22,844
So I told my teammates

515
00:29:22,927 --> 00:29:24,387
that we were going for Australia.

516
00:29:24,971 --> 00:29:26,556
They're talking about coming at us, right?

517
00:29:26,639 --> 00:29:27,640
-Türkiye?
-Yeah.

518
00:29:27,724 --> 00:29:30,351
Yeah, they're like, looking at us
and talking back to their team.

519
00:29:30,435 --> 00:29:31,644
Talk all you want.

520
00:29:31,728 --> 00:29:33,313
But bring it to action and beat us.

521
00:29:33,396 --> 00:29:34,731
Show us what you got.

522
00:29:35,273 --> 00:29:38,860
If it's a one-on-one, we can beat Korea.

523
00:29:38,943 --> 00:29:41,154
-I'm sure we can beat Korea.
-Yeah.

524
00:29:41,946 --> 00:29:45,158
When it came to who to take on,

525
00:29:45,241 --> 00:29:47,619
our only option was Korea.

526
00:29:47,702 --> 00:29:49,537
We needed to take them out in this round.

527
00:29:50,163 --> 00:29:52,290
We need to take the safe route
and go for Japan.

528
00:29:52,373 --> 00:29:54,584
If we go for Australia,
Japan will get a free pass.

529
00:29:55,168 --> 00:29:57,337
Japan and Australia have
the least experience in this game,

530
00:29:57,420 --> 00:29:58,797
so they're the easy targets.

531
00:29:59,339 --> 00:30:01,007
We can beat them without a problem.

532
00:30:01,841 --> 00:30:02,759
Ready…

533
00:30:04,761 --> 00:30:07,013
LOCATION SELECTION

534
00:30:07,680 --> 00:30:08,932
Come on.

535
00:30:11,142 --> 00:30:12,727
All right, let's do this!

536
00:30:14,145 --> 00:30:15,647
All four countries

537
00:30:15,730 --> 00:30:18,107
have now selected their starting points.

538
00:30:19,275 --> 00:30:20,401
Türkiye's on our scent now.

539
00:30:20,485 --> 00:30:21,444
-Sweet.
-Yeah, perfect.

540
00:30:21,528 --> 00:30:22,654
I don't think they want us though.

541
00:30:22,737 --> 00:30:24,239
No, Türkiye's not…

542
00:30:25,114 --> 00:30:27,575
This is going to be a clash
between two powerhouses.

543
00:30:27,659 --> 00:30:29,786
They're staring us down.

544
00:30:29,869 --> 00:30:30,954
Who cares?

545
00:30:32,372 --> 00:30:34,040
Let them stare. We're not going anywhere.

546
00:30:35,458 --> 00:30:38,002
Thank goodness. We got Korea.

547
00:30:38,628 --> 00:30:39,754
This is the showdown.

548
00:30:39,838 --> 00:30:41,381
It'll be an easy win for us.

549
00:30:42,423 --> 00:30:44,717
Good fight.

550
00:30:45,760 --> 00:30:47,804
Good fight.

551
00:30:51,307 --> 00:30:53,393
There's no way we're losing to Korea.

552
00:30:53,476 --> 00:30:54,894
We'll win, no matter what.

553
00:30:55,395 --> 00:30:57,647
If we win, we're moving up to the final.

554
00:30:57,730 --> 00:30:58,773
Republic of Korea!

555
00:30:58,857 --> 00:31:00,149
-Let's go!
-Let's go!

556
00:31:01,234 --> 00:31:02,151
One, two, three!

557
00:31:02,235 --> 00:31:03,403
-Go Japan!
-Go Japan!

558
00:31:06,364 --> 00:31:07,323
Stand by.

559
00:31:10,577 --> 00:31:11,494
We got this, guys.

560
00:31:11,578 --> 00:31:12,745
-Make it count.
-Let's do this.

561
00:31:15,373 --> 00:31:17,041
Ready? Here we go.

562
00:31:19,210 --> 00:31:20,211
Ready…

563
00:31:20,753 --> 00:31:22,046
Size against skill.

564
00:31:22,130 --> 00:31:23,464
That's like, insane.

565
00:31:24,340 --> 00:31:27,093
This is going to be a brutal showdown.

566
00:31:27,176 --> 00:31:30,597
I'm so nervous,
my heart's pounding out of my chest.

567
00:31:34,309 --> 00:31:36,352
Let's go, let's go!

568
00:31:56,289 --> 00:31:58,249
It was like crashing
into a brick wall. "Bam!"

569
00:31:58,333 --> 00:32:00,418
He wasn't just huge, he was also skilled.

570
00:32:00,501 --> 00:32:02,712
He looked incredibly powerful.

571
00:32:10,428 --> 00:32:13,431
This is a legendary battle.

572
00:32:18,811 --> 00:32:20,563
This is next-level.

573
00:32:20,647 --> 00:32:21,856
Damn, straight into a brawl.

574
00:32:29,447 --> 00:32:30,865
-Did the judo guy pin him down?
-Yeah.

575
00:32:30,949 --> 00:32:32,992
Oh, they're all tied up. Wow.

576
00:32:34,827 --> 00:32:36,120
Sit down. Okay, good.

577
00:32:36,204 --> 00:32:38,164
-Anyone not secured?
-Seung-yeon, grab onto me.

578
00:32:38,247 --> 00:32:39,082
Yeah, that's it.

579
00:32:40,792 --> 00:32:41,751
Hold here and hold tight.

580
00:32:45,338 --> 00:32:47,131
No, let go of me. I'm pulling away.

581
00:32:52,804 --> 00:32:54,597
-Okay.
-Min-jae, you've got to get in here.

582
00:32:54,681 --> 00:32:55,890
Min-jae, you've got to get in here.

583
00:32:58,893 --> 00:33:00,687
I've got him. Get him out here!

584
00:33:00,770 --> 00:33:01,771
-Go!
-Get the judo guy out here.

585
00:33:02,397 --> 00:33:05,316
I thought the guy was small enough,
so I tried to throw him,

586
00:33:05,400 --> 00:33:06,567
but then he pulled a judo move,

587
00:33:06,651 --> 00:33:08,069
and I was just trapped.

588
00:33:08,152 --> 00:33:10,238
The judo guy was no joke.

589
00:33:10,321 --> 00:33:11,698
I had to change tack.

590
00:33:11,781 --> 00:33:13,574
I decided my only option
was to keep him outside with me.

591
00:33:13,658 --> 00:33:14,701
KIM MIN-JAE
SSIREUM WRESTLER

592
00:33:14,784 --> 00:33:17,328
I felt like a kid fighting an adult.

593
00:33:17,412 --> 00:33:19,122
SOICHI HASHIMOTO
NATIONAL TEAM JUDOKA

594
00:33:19,205 --> 00:33:23,251
But I'm used to going against
large opponents in judo,

595
00:33:23,334 --> 00:33:25,586
so I'm sure I can handle him.

596
00:33:35,722 --> 00:33:36,597
Get out of here.

597
00:33:38,099 --> 00:33:39,017
Get out of here.

598
00:33:49,402 --> 00:33:51,571
I'm 43 years old,

599
00:33:51,654 --> 00:33:53,281
and the game really wore me out.

600
00:33:54,073 --> 00:33:56,576
The Australian team is strong.

601
00:33:56,659 --> 00:33:58,286
But I kept going.

602
00:33:58,369 --> 00:34:00,246
I'm hoping we'll win.

603
00:34:02,290 --> 00:34:03,124
Hold me.

604
00:34:03,207 --> 00:34:05,835
-I got you.
-Hold me.

605
00:34:08,254 --> 00:34:09,255
I'll stay here.

606
00:34:11,174 --> 00:34:12,383
Yeah, just come back.

607
00:34:18,181 --> 00:34:20,725
Looking over at Türkiye,
I could tell they wanted it.

608
00:34:22,310 --> 00:34:23,936
But I felt like we were gonna win.

609
00:34:27,482 --> 00:34:28,691
Got a minute left.

610
00:34:36,449 --> 00:34:38,284
Hold on.

611
00:34:38,367 --> 00:34:40,244
Hold on. Okay.

612
00:34:42,580 --> 00:34:44,123
Let's back Sung-bin. We'll push him.

613
00:34:44,207 --> 00:34:45,750
Amotti, shift your knee around.

614
00:34:45,833 --> 00:34:47,293
Hold on. I can't.

615
00:34:47,376 --> 00:34:48,419
Sung-bin's picked him up!

616
00:34:49,921 --> 00:34:51,297
Sung-bin's picked him up!

617
00:34:55,176 --> 00:34:56,511
Oh, my swimmer…

618
00:34:57,095 --> 00:34:58,638
Sung-bin's picked him up!

619
00:34:58,721 --> 00:34:59,764
Throw him down.

620
00:35:10,191 --> 00:35:12,485
-There's still time, Sung-bin. It's okay.
-Fifty seconds!

621
00:35:12,568 --> 00:35:14,529
It's all right.

622
00:35:15,113 --> 00:35:16,114
Watch the time!

623
00:35:16,197 --> 00:35:17,448
Get in there in time!

624
00:35:18,032 --> 00:35:19,242
Forty-five seconds.

625
00:35:19,325 --> 00:35:20,201
Hang in there.

626
00:35:20,785 --> 00:35:22,120
They've got a hold of me.

627
00:35:23,204 --> 00:35:24,372
Seung-yeon, hold onto me tight.

628
00:35:24,455 --> 00:35:25,289
Just keep holding on.

629
00:35:28,793 --> 00:35:30,336
Min-jae, keep holding him down!

630
00:35:30,962 --> 00:35:32,296
Just 40 more seconds!

631
00:35:36,384 --> 00:35:37,385
Hold.

632
00:35:39,011 --> 00:35:42,849
It's really tough, but the more you play,

633
00:35:43,474 --> 00:35:45,476
the more adrenaline kicks in.

634
00:35:48,187 --> 00:35:49,689
The hard thing was,

635
00:35:49,772 --> 00:35:53,276
one of their girls ran straight up
and tried to take…

636
00:35:53,985 --> 00:35:55,319
There was still time.

637
00:35:55,403 --> 00:35:57,155
And I was fired up to the max.

638
00:36:02,618 --> 00:36:04,162
No way. She's fighting two huge men.

639
00:36:04,245 --> 00:36:05,788
Well, she is a world champion.

640
00:36:11,043 --> 00:36:12,086
Thirty seconds.

641
00:36:12,962 --> 00:36:15,631
-Thirty seconds!
-Come on, thirty seconds!

642
00:36:15,715 --> 00:36:17,091
They're turning it around.

643
00:36:17,175 --> 00:36:19,719
Sung-bin, come back in 30 seconds.
I'll watch the time for you.

644
00:36:23,681 --> 00:36:25,391
He was much stronger than I expected,

645
00:36:25,474 --> 00:36:28,853
even despite being much lighter than me.

646
00:36:28,936 --> 00:36:31,480
I was completely overwhelmed by his power,

647
00:36:31,564 --> 00:36:34,358
and all I could do
was stay on the defensive.

648
00:36:37,695 --> 00:36:38,946
Fifteen seconds.

649
00:36:39,030 --> 00:36:40,281
Last 15 seconds.

650
00:36:40,364 --> 00:36:41,407
It's three to three either way.

651
00:36:46,370 --> 00:36:47,747
Are you guys all on here?

652
00:36:48,664 --> 00:36:49,582
Nefise!

653
00:36:50,166 --> 00:36:51,125
Get up! You have to come!

654
00:36:54,170 --> 00:36:55,421
Go to Anıl!

655
00:36:55,504 --> 00:36:56,380
On!

656
00:36:59,133 --> 00:36:59,967
Get on this.

657
00:37:02,261 --> 00:37:03,304
Get off it.

658
00:37:04,222 --> 00:37:05,556
Ten seconds.

659
00:37:06,098 --> 00:37:08,100
-Let's go!
-Let's go, come on!

660
00:37:08,184 --> 00:37:09,602
Recep! We need one more!

661
00:37:09,685 --> 00:37:10,686
We only have seven seconds.

662
00:37:11,229 --> 00:37:12,271
Five seconds!

663
00:37:14,357 --> 00:37:15,900
It ends here!

664
00:37:15,983 --> 00:37:18,110
Come on, finish it off! Push one off!

665
00:37:18,736 --> 00:37:21,197
The plan was to leave him there
and get back in,

666
00:37:21,280 --> 00:37:22,531
but it didn't work out.

667
00:37:25,576 --> 00:37:27,161
Four! Three!

668
00:37:27,245 --> 00:37:28,663
Two! One!

669
00:37:30,957 --> 00:37:32,041
All right!

670
00:37:34,168 --> 00:37:35,336
Did we win?

671
00:37:35,419 --> 00:37:36,671
-No.
-What happened?

672
00:37:36,754 --> 00:37:38,798
-Same-same.
-What about over there?

673
00:37:38,881 --> 00:37:40,299
Damn, did Türkiye win?

674
00:37:40,383 --> 00:37:41,509
Australia won?

675
00:37:41,592 --> 00:37:42,551
I think so.

676
00:37:43,552 --> 00:37:45,554
7 SECONDS AGO

677
00:37:45,638 --> 00:37:48,015
Five seconds!

678
00:37:48,599 --> 00:37:50,017
Guys, four seconds to go!

679
00:37:50,101 --> 00:37:51,936
Three! Two!

680
00:38:15,459 --> 00:38:16,585
Türkiye won?

681
00:38:17,586 --> 00:38:18,754
Türkiye wins.

682
00:38:18,838 --> 00:38:20,840
-No.
-Yes.

683
00:38:25,344 --> 00:38:27,346
Here are the countries
surviving after the second round.

684
00:38:28,097 --> 00:38:29,140
Türkiye.

685
00:38:30,933 --> 00:38:32,018
Gather up.

686
00:38:34,603 --> 00:38:36,772
-One, two, three, Türkiye!
-One, two, three, Türkiye!

687
00:38:36,856 --> 00:38:38,733
-Bravo!
-Good round.

688
00:38:40,443 --> 00:38:43,362
I feel guilty for that,

689
00:38:43,446 --> 00:38:45,740
because everyone else was on there,

690
00:38:45,823 --> 00:38:48,701
and I was not on there.

691
00:38:48,784 --> 00:38:51,454
I really felt like I let my team down

692
00:38:51,537 --> 00:38:55,499
and just felt so horrible after that.

693
00:38:55,583 --> 00:38:59,086
I knew I never wanted to
feel that feeling again.

694
00:39:00,004 --> 00:39:01,547
They had a great game plan.

695
00:39:01,630 --> 00:39:04,633
Like, I gotta give them
respect and props when it's due.

696
00:39:04,717 --> 00:39:07,261
But I'm very proud of my team,
the way we came together,

697
00:39:07,345 --> 00:39:10,056
the heart they all showed,
the heart we all showed.

698
00:39:10,598 --> 00:39:12,558
It was like we'd just won
the final or something.

699
00:39:12,641 --> 00:39:13,517
NEFISE KARATAY
FORMER NATIONAL TRACK ATHLETE

700
00:39:13,601 --> 00:39:16,520
Our game plan was spot on.

701
00:39:16,604 --> 00:39:18,898
The Australians were completely shocked.

702
00:39:18,981 --> 00:39:20,441
I'm so proud and happy right now.

703
00:39:20,524 --> 00:39:21,776
YASEMIN ADAR YIĞIT
NATIONAL TEAM WRESTLER

704
00:39:21,859 --> 00:39:23,861
I'm overwhelmed with emotion.

705
00:39:23,944 --> 00:39:25,780
I'm so proud of us.

706
00:39:26,405 --> 00:39:27,406
Rematch.

707
00:39:28,366 --> 00:39:30,493
Korea versus Japan.

708
00:39:32,536 --> 00:39:33,746
Sorry, guys.

709
00:39:33,829 --> 00:39:35,831
Doing like 17 matches today.

710
00:39:36,457 --> 00:39:37,458
Crazy.

711
00:39:37,541 --> 00:39:38,709
We have to go again.

712
00:39:39,627 --> 00:39:41,170
Seriously, what do we need to do
to pull ahead?

713
00:39:41,253 --> 00:39:42,088
I know.

714
00:39:42,171 --> 00:39:44,757
Kim Dong-hyun and the big ssireum guy.

715
00:39:44,840 --> 00:39:46,258
Korea is unbeatable

716
00:39:46,342 --> 00:39:48,386
as long as they're still around.

717
00:39:48,469 --> 00:39:51,263
We need to deal with those two first.

718
00:39:51,347 --> 00:39:52,890
KIM MIN-JAE
SSIREUM WRESTLER

719
00:39:52,973 --> 00:39:56,310
I was annoyed that I couldn't get away
because Soichi had me held down.

720
00:39:56,394 --> 00:39:59,188
I'm definitely going to get him
in the next match.

721
00:40:02,149 --> 00:40:04,527
Second round of the territory conquest.

722
00:40:05,569 --> 00:40:07,488
The rematch will now begin.

723
00:40:08,781 --> 00:40:11,075
The game will last for one minute.

724
00:40:12,201 --> 00:40:13,911
-The Republic of Korea…
-Let's go.

725
00:40:13,994 --> 00:40:15,496
Let's make this the last.

726
00:40:15,579 --> 00:40:16,622
…versus Japan.

727
00:40:18,249 --> 00:40:19,542
Let's go!

728
00:40:19,625 --> 00:40:21,210
Let's get it!

729
00:40:21,293 --> 00:40:23,462
Go, Korea!

730
00:40:23,546 --> 00:40:25,506
I wonder if Korea's just gonna bow down.

731
00:40:25,589 --> 00:40:26,632
That's fine.

732
00:40:26,715 --> 00:40:28,092
Oh, no. They've got Big Boy.

733
00:40:28,175 --> 00:40:29,301
Yeah.

734
00:40:29,385 --> 00:40:31,387
-Korea's got Big Boy.
-Yeah.

735
00:40:31,470 --> 00:40:32,888
But Japan's got fighters.

736
00:40:33,681 --> 00:40:34,515
Yeah.

737
00:40:36,058 --> 00:40:37,059
Stand by.

738
00:40:37,143 --> 00:40:39,145
All right, here we go. Run.

739
00:40:39,895 --> 00:40:40,896
I'll block this side.

740
00:40:42,106 --> 00:40:43,023
This is the final minute.

741
00:40:46,152 --> 00:40:46,986
Ready…

742
00:41:14,013 --> 00:41:15,890
Given Itoi's imposing physique,

743
00:41:15,973 --> 00:41:18,726
I knew he'd be strong.

744
00:41:18,809 --> 00:41:20,394
But he surpassed my expectations.

745
00:41:22,229 --> 00:41:23,689
I just couldn't get him off me.

746
00:41:27,818 --> 00:41:28,903
Who is this?

747
00:41:28,986 --> 00:41:30,738
Who is he carrying off?

748
00:41:42,041 --> 00:41:44,084
-Who is this?
-Who's the guy?

749
00:41:44,168 --> 00:41:46,086
-Oh, he's got the swimmer. That's right.
-Oh my god.

750
00:41:46,629 --> 00:41:48,214
Sung-bin!

751
00:41:48,297 --> 00:41:49,840
Holy moly.

752
00:41:52,885 --> 00:41:54,512
Sung-bin's throwing him down the hill.

753
00:41:55,054 --> 00:41:56,096
Hold him!

754
00:41:58,432 --> 00:42:02,019
I was terrified by his beastlike strength.

755
00:42:02,102 --> 00:42:03,896
But looking around me,

756
00:42:04,522 --> 00:42:08,400
I could see all my teammates
trying their best to push back.

757
00:42:09,652 --> 00:42:13,280
Seeing that,
I was determined to hold him off

758
00:42:13,364 --> 00:42:15,658
no matter what it took.

759
00:42:17,910 --> 00:42:19,078
Thirty seconds.

760
00:42:21,705 --> 00:42:23,207
All right, I'm on it.

761
00:42:23,290 --> 00:42:25,751
Min-jae, stop him from getting on!

762
00:42:27,211 --> 00:42:28,254
Come on, block him.

763
00:42:35,886 --> 00:42:36,887
Put your strength into it.

764
00:42:38,013 --> 00:42:38,973
Use your knees.

765
00:42:43,060 --> 00:42:45,896
You can grab at me all you want,
but you can't pull me off.

766
00:42:52,403 --> 00:42:53,779
Ten seconds.

767
00:42:53,862 --> 00:42:54,905
Come on. Ten, nine…

768
00:42:54,989 --> 00:42:56,949
Come on!

769
00:43:09,128 --> 00:43:10,921
Five! Four!

770
00:43:11,005 --> 00:43:12,423
Dong-hyun, get up here.

771
00:43:13,132 --> 00:43:14,550
Dong-hyun, get up here.

772
00:43:20,598 --> 00:43:21,724
Stop.

773
00:43:21,807 --> 00:43:23,017
Game over.

774
00:43:25,185 --> 00:43:26,770
Okay, one more!

775
00:43:26,854 --> 00:43:27,980
Let's do this once more.

776
00:43:33,402 --> 00:43:36,572
-One more!
-One more!

777
00:43:37,156 --> 00:43:39,533
Yes, Japan! Let's go!

778
00:43:44,330 --> 00:43:46,665
Here was the real bummer.

779
00:43:47,875 --> 00:43:49,209
I grabbed Okami,

780
00:43:49,293 --> 00:43:52,838
got up, and flipped him over
before jumping onto the territory

781
00:43:52,921 --> 00:43:54,923
with two seconds to go.

782
00:43:55,007 --> 00:43:57,176
But he still managed to get on.

783
00:43:58,218 --> 00:43:59,803
He was strong, as expected.

784
00:43:59,887 --> 00:44:03,766
It's not that I wasn't moving,
but that I couldn't move.

785
00:44:03,849 --> 00:44:06,977
So it was a tie,
and we were back to square one.

786
00:44:07,061 --> 00:44:10,189
No matter what we did,
we just couldn't pull ahead.

787
00:44:11,315 --> 00:44:12,316
Rematch.

788
00:44:13,400 --> 00:44:15,653
The Republic of Korea versus Japan.

789
00:44:16,945 --> 00:44:19,156
We got this. It's all about willpower.

790
00:44:19,239 --> 00:44:20,908
-Yeah!
-Come on!

791
00:44:23,786 --> 00:44:25,996
They're not having a good time, Korea.

792
00:44:26,538 --> 00:44:28,791
Korea's just on a rematch bender.

793
00:44:28,874 --> 00:44:32,294
It shows their willingness
to be on the platform.

794
00:44:32,378 --> 00:44:34,880
Are we going to sit on the sidelines
watching Japan play?

795
00:44:34,963 --> 00:44:37,216
When we're the stars of the show?
This is our show.

796
00:44:37,299 --> 00:44:38,300
Stand by.

797
00:44:38,384 --> 00:44:40,719
One minute is all it takes.
They're even more drained than us.

798
00:44:41,428 --> 00:44:42,388
Ready…

799
00:45:01,573 --> 00:45:04,201
All right. I see you.

800
00:45:09,164 --> 00:45:10,874
Let's go, Sung-bin!

801
00:45:17,840 --> 00:45:18,674
Oh, single!

802
00:45:19,299 --> 00:45:20,384
Nice single leg.

803
00:45:22,219 --> 00:45:24,972
That's it! Come on!

804
00:45:25,055 --> 00:45:26,265
Don't let go!

805
00:45:27,683 --> 00:45:29,101
Hold him down!

806
00:45:31,687 --> 00:45:34,314
-Pin him!
-That's my guy!

807
00:45:36,066 --> 00:45:39,862
He was just mind-blowingly strong.

808
00:45:39,945 --> 00:45:44,741
You see, I'd seen Nakamura get carried off

809
00:45:44,825 --> 00:45:47,578
by Yun Sung-bin in the previous match.

810
00:45:48,120 --> 00:45:51,165
So I thought,
"Why do I have to face him? Why me?"

811
00:45:53,125 --> 00:45:54,334
Thirty seconds.

812
00:45:56,128 --> 00:45:57,963
What's going on? How many are there?

813
00:45:59,089 --> 00:46:01,508
They're tied.

814
00:46:02,468 --> 00:46:04,470
Go, go! Get her off!

815
00:46:10,100 --> 00:46:11,268
Hold on, I'm going to fall off.

816
00:46:12,728 --> 00:46:14,146
Dong-hyun, we've got 20 seconds.

817
00:46:17,024 --> 00:46:18,233
Push her to the other side.

818
00:46:18,942 --> 00:46:19,902
Seung-yeon, come here.

819
00:46:28,619 --> 00:46:29,703
Ten seconds.

820
00:46:31,163 --> 00:46:32,831
Ten seconds!

821
00:46:36,627 --> 00:46:38,128
-Push him off!
-Push him off!

822
00:46:38,212 --> 00:46:39,546
Min-jae, push him off!

823
00:46:39,630 --> 00:46:41,006
-Push him off!
-Push him off!

824
00:46:42,132 --> 00:46:43,675
-Push him off!
-Push him off!

825
00:46:45,010 --> 00:46:46,470
Four! Three!

826
00:46:46,553 --> 00:46:48,055
Just get his feet to touch the ground!

827
00:46:54,853 --> 00:46:57,189
Stop. Game over.

828
00:47:03,320 --> 00:47:04,363
So close, Min-jae.

829
00:47:05,364 --> 00:47:06,532
It's a draw.

830
00:47:07,157 --> 00:47:08,367
-It's a draw.
-A draw?

831
00:47:08,450 --> 00:47:09,284
A draw.

832
00:47:10,369 --> 00:47:13,121
By then, I was thinking,
"When will this be over?"

833
00:47:14,456 --> 00:47:17,960
It didn't seem like
it was going to be over anytime soon.

834
00:47:18,835 --> 00:47:22,548
There was nothing to do except gather
every last ounce of willpower

835
00:47:22,631 --> 00:47:24,466
and keep going until they folded.

836
00:47:25,884 --> 00:47:26,802
Rematch.

837
00:47:28,470 --> 00:47:30,055
-Ready…
-Let's go.

838
00:47:30,138 --> 00:47:31,098
One minute is all it is.

839
00:47:34,851 --> 00:47:37,771
It was just one rematch after another,

840
00:47:37,854 --> 00:47:41,024
and both teams fought tooth and nail
with neither side giving ground.

841
00:47:42,067 --> 00:47:43,944
Neither side
was willing to give up or concede.

842
00:47:47,364 --> 00:47:48,949
I thought, "We can't lose this."

843
00:47:49,032 --> 00:47:50,784
"We'll win this, even if it kills us."

844
00:47:53,662 --> 00:47:56,039
Stop. Game over.

845
00:47:56,873 --> 00:47:57,708
Not again.

846
00:47:58,792 --> 00:47:59,960
It's just not working.

847
00:48:00,544 --> 00:48:01,628
It just wouldn't end.

848
00:48:02,629 --> 00:48:03,630
Ready…

849
00:48:08,343 --> 00:48:11,138
It was really tough, to be honest.

850
00:48:11,805 --> 00:48:15,559
I was truly at the end of my rope.

851
00:48:16,852 --> 00:48:18,854
I'd reached my limit

852
00:48:19,521 --> 00:48:21,773
both mentally and physically.

853
00:48:24,610 --> 00:48:25,652
Stop.

854
00:48:25,736 --> 00:48:27,029
Game over.

855
00:48:34,578 --> 00:48:36,330
I looked around at my teammates,

856
00:48:36,413 --> 00:48:38,290
and they still had that fire in them.

857
00:48:39,666 --> 00:48:42,544
It strengthened my resolve to beat Japan.

858
00:48:44,504 --> 00:48:46,632
Our team is completely wrecked,

859
00:48:46,715 --> 00:48:50,010
but we're going to muster
every last bit of strength to win this.

860
00:48:53,347 --> 00:48:54,473
Stop.

861
00:48:54,556 --> 00:48:55,682
Game over.

862
00:49:02,814 --> 00:49:05,317
It's just never-ending.

863
00:49:06,151 --> 00:49:10,364
A new rule was brought in
because it kept dragging on

864
00:49:10,447 --> 00:49:12,824
with no end in sight.

865
00:49:12,908 --> 00:49:15,619
Those who were pushed off the territory

866
00:49:15,702 --> 00:49:18,080
could no longer reenter.

867
00:49:18,163 --> 00:49:20,374
Whichever team had more players remaining

868
00:49:20,457 --> 00:49:23,126
after the minute was up
would be the winner.

869
00:49:23,210 --> 00:49:25,379
However, the heaviest

870
00:49:25,462 --> 00:49:28,340
and the lightest players on each team

871
00:49:28,423 --> 00:49:31,385
were excluded from the match.

872
00:49:31,468 --> 00:49:34,388
So based on those rules,

873
00:49:34,471 --> 00:49:35,639
it became a four-on-four game.

874
00:49:38,350 --> 00:49:40,560
I think they're all starting on there.

875
00:49:40,644 --> 00:49:42,104
A four-on-four.

876
00:49:42,187 --> 00:49:43,271
Sudden death.

877
00:49:44,189 --> 00:49:46,024
You've got to push me from behind, okay?

878
00:49:46,108 --> 00:49:46,942
They'll be charging at us.

879
00:49:47,484 --> 00:49:49,069
It might be better to dodge them.

880
00:49:49,152 --> 00:49:50,612
No, we're going to charge.

881
00:49:53,532 --> 00:49:54,366
Stand by.

882
00:49:54,449 --> 00:49:55,367
Keep your stance low.

883
00:49:57,327 --> 00:49:59,788
It's a matter of national pride.
We must defeat Japan.

884
00:50:00,872 --> 00:50:03,125
We've got to do this.
Losing is not an option.

885
00:50:06,712 --> 00:50:07,879
Now. Lock together now.

886
00:50:16,179 --> 00:50:17,764
Sung-bin's on the edge there.

887
00:50:24,271 --> 00:50:27,607
YUN SUNG-BIN OF THE REPUBLIC OF KOREA
& YOSHIO OF JAPAN ARE OUT

888
00:50:27,691 --> 00:50:28,817
There it is. Go, go.

889
00:50:29,985 --> 00:50:31,069
-Gone.
-There you go.

890
00:50:37,367 --> 00:50:39,953
AMOTTI OF THE REPUBLIC OF KOREA
& KATSUMI OF JAPAN ARE OUT

891
00:50:40,495 --> 00:50:42,164
You've got to push someone out!

892
00:50:47,335 --> 00:50:50,255
KIM DONG-HYUN OF THE REPUBLIC OF KOREA
& SOICHI OF JAPAN ARE OUT

893
00:50:50,797 --> 00:50:53,633
Amotti and I fell off at the same time,

894
00:50:53,717 --> 00:50:55,761
making it a one-on-one between two girls.

895
00:50:56,303 --> 00:50:58,388
We realized this had been
Japan's game plan all along.

896
00:50:58,472 --> 00:51:00,807
They wanted a one-on-one
between the girls.

897
00:51:01,433 --> 00:51:02,893
One-on-one.

898
00:51:02,976 --> 00:51:05,145
-No way.
-One-on-one.

899
00:51:12,903 --> 00:51:14,196
This is so cool.

900
00:51:14,738 --> 00:51:16,823
One versus one. Girls are in.

901
00:51:16,907 --> 00:51:18,784
Red's CrossFit,

902
00:51:18,867 --> 00:51:20,410
and then Blue is…

903
00:51:20,494 --> 00:51:21,787
-Wrestling.
-Wrestling, yeah.

904
00:51:22,537 --> 00:51:23,955
Brute strength versus skill.

905
00:51:24,039 --> 00:51:26,333
-Brute strength versus skill.
-Let's see.

906
00:51:27,042 --> 00:51:29,169
We were confident that Ozaki,

907
00:51:29,711 --> 00:51:33,340
Japan's star wrestler, would win.

908
00:51:33,423 --> 00:51:37,511
So this had gone
exactly according to plan.

909
00:51:38,386 --> 00:51:40,639
Since I'm a wrestler,

910
00:51:40,722 --> 00:51:43,141
I believed I had the upper hand.

911
00:51:43,225 --> 00:51:44,601
I had full confidence.

912
00:51:45,936 --> 00:51:47,229
Come on, Seung-yeon. Let's do this.

913
00:51:47,312 --> 00:51:48,438
-All right.
-You got this!

914
00:51:48,522 --> 00:51:51,024
When it ended up as a one-on-one,

915
00:51:51,107 --> 00:51:53,318
Team Japan acted
as if victory was already theirs.

916
00:51:53,401 --> 00:51:56,571
And I kind of like it
when people underestimate me.

917
00:51:56,655 --> 00:51:59,866
It gets me fired up.

918
00:51:59,950 --> 00:52:03,995
So I thought,
"Okay, I'll have to win this then."

919
00:52:08,542 --> 00:52:09,584
Stand by.

920
00:52:12,003 --> 00:52:15,215
I'm going to drag you off, no matter what.

921
00:52:16,049 --> 00:52:18,635
I'm fired up with grit.
I want to win this so bad.

922
00:52:20,303 --> 00:52:21,221
Ready…

923
00:54:23,551 --> 00:54:28,556
Subtitle translation by: Jee Butcher

